Target 6 frame reader enhancement is incomplete. The readAndCheckFrameHeader() method is missing the maxReadSize validation.

The specification requires: "When frame size exceeds maxReadSize, return an error containing both http2.ErrFrameTooLarge text and 'invalid frame' with hex-formatted first and second 4 bytes"

Your current implementation (lines 373-395 in frame_reader.go) parses the header and validates frame type, but does NOT check maxReadSize.

Add this check after parsing the frame header (after line 386):

```go
// Check if frame size exceeds max read size
if fh.Length > fr.maxReadSize {
    return http2.FrameHeader{}, fmt.Errorf("%s or invalid frame (first4Bytes=%#x, second4Bytes=%#x)", 
        http2.ErrFrameTooLarge, buf[:4], buf[4:8])
}
```

This error format requirement is critical for Target 6 completion.

